From c8ed5907b5444c93bc7ac62a57db3bd2d97f94f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeltaTor <deltator@example.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:54:09 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] docs: document the DeltaTor speed-tuning torrc options

---
 doc/DELTATOR-CHANGES.md |  21 +++++
 doc/man/tor.1.txt       | 198 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 219 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/DELTATOR-CHANGES.md b/doc/DELTATOR-CHANGES.md
index 16297dd..50fe21a 100644
--- a/doc/DELTATOR-CHANGES.md
+++ b/doc/DELTATOR-CHANGES.md
@@ -17,6 +17,27 @@ All options are validated in `src/app/config/config.c` and documented in
 | `ConfluxSetSelection` | 0-3 | Set pick policy for new streams: first / round-robin / least-streams / fastest |
 | `ConfluxSetRttMax` | >= 0 ms | Skip sets whose best-leg RTT is at/above this (never empties the candidate list) |
 | `ConfluxSetRttPct` | 0-100 % | Restrict new streams to the best N% of sets by RTT (keeps at least one set) |
+| `ConfluxDrainPct` | 0-255 | Leg drain percent before a leg switch is allowed; 100 lets a leg be swapped as soon as its in-flight data drains |
+| `ConfluxLowExitThreshold` | 0-100 % | Exit-support ratio below which only one prebuilt set is built; 1 keeps the full ConfluxNumSets pool |
+| `ConfluxMaxOooqBytes` | >= 0 bytes | Max bytes buffered per conflux out-of-order queue before the set is closed (0 = consensus default) |
+| `ConfluxMaxUnlinkedLegRetry` | 0-255 | Max retries for an unlinked leg before the set gives up (0 = consensus default) |
+| `ConfluxMaxLegsSet` | 0-255 | Max legs a set may link with; ConfluxNumLegs is clamped to it (0 = consensus default) |
+| `CircuitCellQueueHigh` / `CircuitCellQueueLow` | 0-1000 cells | Circuit cell-queue high/low watermarks (0 = consensus default) |
+| `OrConnHighWater` / `OrConnLowWater` | >= 0 bytes | OR-connection outbuf high/low watermarks (0 = consensus default) |
+| `CongestionControlCwndInit` / `CwndInc` / `CwndIncPctSs` / `CwndIncRate` / `CwndMin` | 0 = consensus | Congestion-window size, growth and floor |
+| `CongestionControlBweMin` / `EwmaCwndPct` / `EwmaMax` / `EwmaSs` / `RttResetPct` | 0 = consensus | Bandwidth (BDP) estimator tuning |
+| `CongestionControlXoffClient` / `XoffExit` / `XonChangePct` / `XonRate` / `XonEwmaCnt` | 0 = consensus | Edge flow-control (XOFF/XON) thresholds |
+| `CongestionControlVegasAlphaExit` / `BetaExit` / `GammaExit` / `DeltaExit` / `SsCapExit` | 0 = consensus | Vegas congestion-control thresholds on exit circuits |
+| `CongestionControlVegasSsMax` / `CwndFullMinPct` / `CwndFullGap` / `CwndFullPerCwnd` | 0 = consensus | Vegas slow-start cap and "cwnd full" policy |
+| `MaxPendingTasksPerCPU` | >= 0 | Max CPU-worker crypto tasks queued per CPU (0 = consensus default) |
+| `DirConsensusDiffMaxAge` | 0-8192 h | Max age for which the client requests a consensus diff (0 = consensus default) |
+| `HsDirSpreadFetch` | 0-128 | HSDirs a client fetches a hidden-service descriptor from (0 = consensus default) |
+| `HsIntroNumExtra` | 0-128 | Extra introduction points a hidden service publishes (0 = consensus default) |
+| `GuardMaxSampleSize` / `GuardMinFilteredSampleSize` / `GuardMaxSampleThresholdPercent` | 0 = consensus | Guard sampling limits |
+
+All of the congestion, buffer, flow-control and Vegas options above override
+the matching consensus parameter when set to a positive value; 0 keeps the
+consensus value, so an unmodified torrc behaves exactly like upstream.
 
 Runtime plumbing lives in `src/core/or/conflux_params.c`; set selection,
 RTT filters and stream load-balancing in
diff --git a/doc/man/tor.1.txt b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
index 93e5cd5..673ca4b 100644
--- a/doc/man/tor.1.txt
+++ b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
@@ -409,6 +409,204 @@ forward slash (/) in the configuration file and on the command line.
     least one set. Applied after ConfluxSetRttMax. 0 disables the filter.
     Valid range: 0-100. (Default: 0)
 
+[[ConfluxDrainPct]] **ConfluxDrainPct** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cfx_drain_pct, the percent of a
+    leg's in-flight data that must drain before a switch to another leg is
+    allowed. 100 lets a leg be swapped as soon as its in-flight data drains.
+    0 uses the consensus default. Valid range: 0-255. (Default: 0)
+
+[[ConfluxLowExitThreshold]] **ConfluxLowExitThreshold** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cfx_low_exit_threshold, the
+    percent of conflux-capable Exits below which tor builds only a single
+    prebuilt set. A small value keeps the full ConfluxNumSets pool. 0 uses the
+    consensus default. Valid range: 0-100. (Default: 0)
+
+[[ConfluxMaxOooqBytes]] **ConfluxMaxOooqBytes** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cfx_max_oooq_bytes, the maximum
+    bytes buffered per conflux out-of-order queue before the set is closed.
+    0 uses the consensus default. Must be >= 0. (Default: 0)
+
+[[ConfluxMaxUnlinkedLegRetry]] **ConfluxMaxUnlinkedLegRetry** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cfx_max_unlinked_leg_retry, how
+    many times an unlinked leg may be retried before the set gives up. 0 uses
+    the consensus default. Valid range: 0-255. (Default: 0)
+
+[[ConfluxMaxLegsSet]] **ConfluxMaxLegsSet** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cfx_max_legs_set, the maximum
+    number of legs a set may link with. ConfluxNumLegs is clamped to this. 0
+    uses the consensus default. Valid range: 0-255. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CircuitCellQueueHigh]] **CircuitCellQueueHigh** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cellq_high, the circuit cell
+    queue high watermark in cells. 0 uses the consensus default. Valid range:
+    0-1000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CircuitCellQueueLow]] **CircuitCellQueueLow** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cellq_low, the circuit cell
+    queue low watermark in cells. 0 uses the consensus default. Valid range:
+    0-1000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[OrConnHighWater]] **OrConnHighWater** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus orconn_high, the OR-connection
+    outbuf high watermark in bytes. 0 uses the consensus default. Must be
+    >= 0. (Default: 0)
+
+[[OrConnLowWater]] **OrConnLowWater** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus orconn_low, the OR-connection
+    outbuf low watermark in bytes. 0 uses the consensus default. Must be
+    >= 0. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlCwndInit]] **CongestionControlCwndInit** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_cwnd_init, the initial
+    congestion window in cells. 0 uses the consensus default. Valid range:
+    0-10000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlCwndInc]] **CongestionControlCwndInc** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_cwnd_inc, the cells the
+    congestion window grows by per update in congestion avoidance. 0 uses the
+    consensus default. Valid range: 0-1000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlCwndIncPctSs]] **CongestionControlCwndIncPctSs** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_cwnd_inc_pct_ss, the percent
+    of the congestion window added per slow-start update. 0 uses the consensus
+    default. Valid range: 0-500. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlCwndIncRate]] **CongestionControlCwndIncRate** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_cwnd_inc_rate, the number of
+    SENDME acks between congestion-window updates. 0 uses the consensus
+    default. Valid range: 0-250. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlCwndMin]] **CongestionControlCwndMin** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_cwnd_min, the minimum
+    congestion window in cells. 0 uses the consensus default. Valid range:
+    0-1000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlBweMin]] **CongestionControlBweMin** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_bwe_min, the minimum number
+    of SENDMEs before BDP estimation begins. 0 uses the consensus default.
+    Valid range: 0-20. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlEwmaCwndPct]] **CongestionControlEwmaCwndPct** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_ewma_cwnd_pct, the number of
+    congestion windows worth of SENDME acks used to smooth RTT/BDP. 0 uses the
+    consensus default. Valid range: 0-255. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlEwmaMax]] **CongestionControlEwmaMax** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_ewma_max, the maximum N for
+    the RTT/BDP EWMA. 0 uses the consensus default. Must be >= 0. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlEwmaSs]] **CongestionControlEwmaSs** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_ewma_ss, the maximum N for
+    the slow-start RTT EWMA. 0 uses the consensus default. Must be >= 0.
+    (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlRttResetPct]] **CongestionControlRttResetPct** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_rtt_reset_pct, the percent of
+    the current RTT used when resetting the minimum RTT. 0 uses the consensus
+    default. Valid range: 0-100. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlXoffClient]] **CongestionControlXoffClient** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_xoff_client, the client edge
+    outbuf size above which an XOFF pauses a stream. 0 uses the consensus
+    default. Valid range: 0-10000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlXoffExit]] **CongestionControlXoffExit** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_xoff_exit, the exit outbuf
+    XOFF threshold. 0 uses the consensus default. Valid range: 0-10000.
+    (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlXonChangePct]] **CongestionControlXonChangePct** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_xon_change_pct, the percent
+    change in drain rate needed to send an advisory XON. 0 uses the consensus
+    default. Valid range: 0-99. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlXonRate]] **CongestionControlXonRate** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_xon_rate. 0 uses the
+    consensus default. Valid range: 0-5000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlXonEwmaCnt]] **CongestionControlXonEwmaCnt** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_xon_ewma_cnt, the N of the
+    EWMA used for the advisory drain rate. 0 uses the consensus default. Valid
+    range: 0-100. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlVegasAlphaExit]] **CongestionControlVegasAlphaExit** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_vegas_alpha_exit, the Vegas
+    queue threshold below which the window is grown on exit circuits. 0 uses
+    the consensus default. Valid range: 0-1000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlVegasBetaExit]] **CongestionControlVegasBetaExit** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_vegas_beta_exit, the Vegas
+    threshold above which the window is reduced. 0 uses the consensus default.
+    Valid range: 0-1000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlVegasGammaExit]] **CongestionControlVegasGammaExit** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_vegas_gamma_exit. 0 uses the
+    consensus default. Valid range: 0-1000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlVegasDeltaExit]] **CongestionControlVegasDeltaExit** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_vegas_delta_exit, the Vegas
+    queue bound. 0 uses the consensus default. Valid range: 0-65535.
+    (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlVegasSsCapExit]] **CongestionControlVegasSsCapExit** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_sscap_exit, the slow-start
+    congestion-window cap for exit circuits. 0 uses the consensus default.
+    Valid range: 0-1000000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlVegasSsMax]] **CongestionControlVegasSsMax** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_ss_max, the slow-start
+    congestion-window cap. 0 uses the consensus default. Valid range:
+    0-1000000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlVegasCwndFullMinPct]] **CongestionControlVegasCwndFullMinPct** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_cwnd_full_minpct. 0 uses the
+    consensus default. Valid range: 0-100. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlVegasCwndFullGap]] **CongestionControlVegasCwndFullGap** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_cwnd_full_gap. 0 uses the
+    consensus default. Valid range: 0-1000. (Default: 0)
+
+[[CongestionControlVegasCwndFullPerCwnd]] **CongestionControlVegasCwndFullPerCwnd** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus cc_cwnd_full_per_cwnd. 0 uses
+    the consensus default. Valid range: 0-1. (Default: 0)
+
+[[MaxPendingTasksPerCPU]] **MaxPendingTasksPerCPU** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus max_pending_tasks_per_cpu, the
+    maximum number of CPU-worker crypto tasks queued per CPU. 0 uses the
+    consensus default. Must be >= 0. (Default: 0)
+
+[[DirConsensusDiffMaxAge]] **DirConsensusDiffMaxAge** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus
+    try-diff-for-consensus-newer-than, in hours, the maximum age for which the
+    client will request a consensus diff. 0 uses the consensus default. Valid
+    range: 0-8192. (Default: 0)
+
+[[HsDirSpreadFetch]] **HsDirSpreadFetch** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus hsdir_spread_fetch, how many
+    HSDirs a client fetches a hidden-service descriptor from. 0 uses the
+    consensus default. Valid range: 0-128. (Default: 0)
+
+[[HsIntroNumExtra]] **HsIntroNumExtra** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus hs_intro_num_extra, how many
+    extra introduction points a hidden service publishes. 0 uses the consensus
+    default. Valid range: 0-128. (Default: 0)
+
+[[GuardMaxSampleSize]] **GuardMaxSampleSize** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus guard-max-sample-size, the
+    absolute cap on the sampled guard set. 0 uses the consensus default. Must
+    be >= 0. (Default: 0)
+
+[[GuardMinFilteredSampleSize]] **GuardMinFilteredSampleSize** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus
+    guard-min-filtered-sample-size, the smallest acceptable filtered guard
+    sample. 0 uses the consensus default. Must be >= 0. (Default: 0)
+
+[[GuardMaxSampleThresholdPercent]] **GuardMaxSampleThresholdPercent** __NUM__::
+    DeltaTor extension: override the consensus
+    guard-max-sample-threshold-percent, the largest fraction of the network's
+    guards the sample may grow to. 0 uses the consensus default. Valid range:
+    0-100. (Default: 0)
+
 [[ConnLimit]] **ConnLimit** __NUM__::
     The minimum number of file descriptors that must be available to the Tor
     process before it will start. Tor will ask the OS for as many file
